# Architecture

Read only the architecture document relevant to the task.

Core invariants:
- Modular monolith; do not introduce microservices by preference.
- Workspace is tenant; users may belong to multiple Workspaces.
- Site belongs to exactly one Workspace.
- Establish ownership before permission; permission and entitlement are separate.
- Global / Workspace / Site scope must be explicit for each persisted domain entity.
- Global Automotive Catalog -> Workspace Vehicle Library -> Site Vehicle/Site Offer.
- Site Offer owns commercial values such as price, benefits, availability and CTA overrides.
- Template definitions never own customer vehicles, prices, integrations or submissions.
- Block Definition -> immutable/versioned Block Version -> Site-owned Block Instance.
- Block runtime uses deterministic schema, not AI parsing of arbitrary HTML.
- Popup and Form are separate concepts.
- Valid Submission is persisted before external Delivery.
- Workspace owns reusable integration credentials; Site owns binding/override configuration.
- Draft != Published; publishing activates a prepared version atomically.
- Third-party/developer blocks never get unrestricted DB/filesystem/env/server execution.

Do not invent or settle unresolved ADRs. If the task depends on one, stop with `BLOCKED_DECISION`.
